<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n110834" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φῐλᾰλήθ-ης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ες</span>
		(parox., on the accent v. Hdn.Gr. <i><span class="en">
			1.80
		</span></i>), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>loving truth, a
				lover of truth,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1127b4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1.361
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				1.76
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.192
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Mar.</u>
				28
			</span></i>; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιλοψεύδης,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Charond.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Stob.
				4.2.24
			</span></i>: 
				Sup.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιλοσοφώτατος καὶ -έστατος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Jul.
					<u>Ep.</u>
					97
				</span></i>
			:—certain philosophers are called <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιλαλήθεις</span> by <i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				1.17
			</span></i>, who seems to intend the Epicureans; also applied to the
			physician Alexander of Laodicea, <i><span class="en">
				Anon.Lond.
				24.32
			</span></i> (where <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φῐλᾰλήθ-ειος</span></b> ), <i><span class="en">
				Sor.
				2.2
			</span></i>, etc. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-θως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Piet.</u>
					123
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				2
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				32
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				19.348
			</span></i>; <i>frankly,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Cic.
				<u>QF</u>
				2.15(16).5
			</span></i>.</div>
